# Copy this file to `.env` (gitignored) and restart `npm start`.
#
# Development only. KindleSync loads `.env` when it is NOT packaged, and only
# reads keys beginning with KINDLESYNC_. An exported shell variable always wins.
# Packaged builds ignore this file and use the values in package.json.
#
# Create a client at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#   1. Create/select a project, then enable the Gmail API.
#   2. Configure the OAuth consent screen (External), add yourself under
#      "Test users", and add the .../auth/gmail.send scope.
#   3. Credentials -> Create credentials -> OAuth client ID -> Desktop app.
KINDLESYNC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Required by Google, despite the name. Google's installed-app flow demands
# client_secret at the token endpoint even when PKCE is used, so sign-in fails
# with "client_secret is missing" without it. RFC 8252 section 8.5 and Google's
# desktop documentation both treat this as a NON-CONFIDENTIAL app identifier:
# it cannot be kept private inside a distributed binary, and PKCE is what
# actually protects the authorization code. Keep it in this gitignored file
# anyway - there is no reason to publish it. Copy it from the same client page
# as the ID above.
KINDLESYNC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
